$DIR/main.p:11:19: cannot use Conn as K in hash.NewSet[Conn]: Conn is an owner and K does not allow owners
    The standard library declares K without owner: its code copies values of K
    freely, so it cannot hold owners. Copying an owner would leave several
    values that all free the same memory.
    Go copies such values freely and its garbage collector frees what they refer
    to when nothing refers to it any more. Plutonium has no garbage collector:
    an owner frees what it owns when it is dropped, so there must be exactly
    one.
    To keep owners in a container, use one that allows them: a vec.Vec holds
    owners, and a hash.Map holds them as its values:
        v := vec.New[Conn]()
    Otherwise use pointers to the owners, or copies made explicitly with Clone.
    (see "Owner types" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.18)
    (run "pluto explain E3207" for a longer explanation)

$DIR/main.p:14:7: cannot use Conn as T in vec.NewFixed: Conn is an owner and T does not allow owners
    The standard library declares T without owner: its code copies values of T
    freely, so it cannot hold owners. Copying an owner would leave several
